{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"005e3a7f-3d0b-4fa2-b542-b3530dfb21b3","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A standing wave forms when two identical waves travel in opposite directions and interfere.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Standing waves"},{"op":"text","id":"idea","region":"A2","content":"opposite waves + interference"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"005e3a7f-3d0b-4fa2-b542-b3530dfb21b3","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Their interference creates fixed nodes and oscillating antinodes along the medium.","ops":[{"op":"sketch","id":"wave","region":"left","strokes":[[[0.05,0.5],[0.12,0.35],[0.19,0.5],[0.26,0.65],[0.33,0.5],[0.4,0.35],[0.47,0.5],[0.54,0.65],[0.61,0.5],[0.68,0.35],[0.75,0.5],[0.82,0.65],[0.89,0.5],[0.95,0.5]],[[0.05,0.5],[0.19,0.5],[0.33,0.5],[0.47,0.5],[0.61,0.5],[0.75,0.5],[0.89,0.5]]]},{"op":"text","id":"nodes","anchor":{"el":"wave","side":"right","gap":0.05},"content":"nodes: no displacement"},{"op":"text","id":"antinodes","anchor":{"el":"wave","side":"below","gap":0.05},"content":"antinodes: maximum displacement"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"What happens at a node?","expected_gist":"The medium remains stationary, with zero displacement."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"005e3a7f-3d0b-4fa2-b542-b3530dfb21b3","step":{"id":"s3","script":"For a string fixed at both ends, only wavelengths fitting an integer number of half-waves are allowed.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"condition","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"L = n\\frac{\\lambda}{2},\\quad n=1,2,3,\\ldots"},{"op":"text","id":"meaning","anchor":{"el":"condition","side":"below","gap":0.05},"content":"n counts the half-waves"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"005e3a7f-3d0b-4fa2-b542-b3530dfb21b3","step":{"id":"s4","script":"The fundamental has one half-wave; higher harmonics add more nodes and antinodes.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"fundamental","anchor":{"el":"condition","side":"right","gap":0.06},"latex":"\\lambda_n=\\frac{2L}{n}"},{"op":"text","id":"summary","anchor":{"el":"fundamental","side":"below","gap":0.05},"content":"larger n: higher frequency"}],"checkpoint":null}}
